{"episode_id":"FE-2b7a9b-mc-signed-feedback-escape","mode":"prospective","source_window_base":"cec27ab2ab7e14ef1ef8e3849412abd6171bd574","source_window_head":"2b7a9b6d8525663ee114e18eaee06419d6286f8a","line":"mobius_cancellation","atlas_territory":"RA-A1","classification":"viable-extension","source_paths":["research/mobius_cancellation/findings/MC-066-signed-squarefree-character-feedback-budget.md"],"basis":"Signed convolution with a squarefree quadratic comparator exactly removes the conductor-zero absolute-transfer floor, isolating a different contractivity resource: a positive power-weighted split-prime feedback budget. This keeps a narrow moving-comparator route alive while making its missing estimate explicit."}
{"episode_id":"FE-2b7a9b-mc-exceptional-feedback-classicalization","mode":"prospective","source_window_base":"cec27ab2ab7e14ef1ef8e3849412abd6171bd574","source_window_head":"2b7a9b6d8525663ee114e18eaee06419d6286f8a","line":"mobius_cancellation","atlas_territory":"RA-A1","classification":"known-prior-art","source_paths":["research/mobius_cancellation/findings/MC-067-siegel-walfisz-polylog-feedback-conductor-barrier.md","research/mobius_cancellation/findings/MC-068-large-sieve-feedback-candidate-sparsity.md","research/mobius_cancellation/findings/MC-069-landau-page-unique-feedback-exception.md"],"basis":"Classical Page-Siegel, large-sieve and Landau-Page mechanisms exclude the positive-feedback condition through stretched-exponential conductor ranges and reduce the wider quasi-subpower family to at most one exceptional primitive character; the apparent family freedom classicalizes rather than yielding a new Mertens estimate."}
{"episode_id":"FE-2b7a9b-pc-refinement-robin-rigidity","mode":"prospective","source_window_base":"cec27ab2ab7e14ef1ef8e3849412abd6171bd574","source_window_head":"2b7a9b6d8525663ee114e18eaee06419d6286f8a","line":"prime_circle","atlas_territory":"RA-G2","classification":"new-barrier","source_paths":["research/prime_circle/findings/PC-166-power-homogeneous-local-metrics-are-flat-log-cylinders.md","research/prime_circle/findings/PC-167-full-refinement-homotheties-rigidify-singular-metrics-to-power-laws.md","research/prime_circle/findings/PC-168-full-refinement-covariance-rigidifies-local-differential-operators.md","research/prime_circle/findings/PC-169-full-refinement-invariant-inverse-square-domains-are-universal-scale-fixed-points.md","research/prime_circle/findings/PC-170-bounded-nonlocal-robin-repairs-are-incompatible-with-exact-power-refinement.md","research/prime_circle/findings/PC-171-strong-refinement-covariant-robin-operators-collapse-to-four-parameters.md"],"basis":"Exact full power-refinement covariance rigidifies local metrics, finite-order operators and inverse-square domains to universal homogeneous models; bounded Robin repair is incompatible with the symmetry and strong unbounded Robin covariance collapses to one fixed four-real-parameter first-order block, leaving no intrinsic shell-dependent arithmetic slot."}
{"episode_id":"FE-2b7a9b-pl-checkpoint-sufficiency","mode":"prospective","source_window_base":"cec27ab2ab7e14ef1ef8e3849412abd6171bd574","source_window_head":"2b7a9b6d8525663ee114e18eaee06419d6286f8a","line":"prime_lattice","atlas_territory":"RA-D1b","classification":"viable-extension","source_paths":["research/prime_lattice/findings/PL-153-suzuki-checkpoint-one-sided-boundedness.md","research/prime_lattice/findings/PL-154-suzuki-checkpoint-zero-frontier-growth-exponent.md","research/prime_lattice/findings/PL-155-two-prime-face-screw-positivity.md","research/prime_lattice/findings/PL-156-ordinary-prime-basis-sampling.md","research/prime_lattice/findings/PL-157-suzuki-generic-sub-three-quarter-mesh.md"],"basis":"Suzuki's completed screw signal can be reduced much further than the continuous criterion: one-sided boundedness on prime-power checkpoints is RH-equivalent and broad sufficiently fine sampling families retain the completed information, isolating observation sufficiency from the still-missing source mechanism."}
{"episode_id":"FE-2b7a9b-pl-fixed-step-aliasing","mode":"prospective","source_window_base":"cec27ab2ab7e14ef1ef8e3849412abd6171bd574","source_window_head":"2b7a9b6d8525663ee114e18eaee06419d6286f8a","line":"prime_lattice","atlas_territory":"RA-D1b","classification":"new-barrier","source_paths":["research/prime_lattice/findings/PL-158-fixed-step-suzuki-offline-aliasing-control.md"],"basis":"Every fixed sampling step admits an exact completed off-line zero quartet whose Suzuki-type screw is one-sided on all sampled points; a single geometric ray therefore has a genuine sampling alias quotient and cannot inherit the continuous one-sided criterion by generic arguments."}
{"episode_id":"FE-2b7a9b-pl-phase-pinned-frontier","mode":"prospective","source_window_base":"cec27ab2ab7e14ef1ef8e3849412abd6171bd574","source_window_head":"2b7a9b6d8525663ee114e18eaee06419d6286f8a","line":"prime_lattice","atlas_territory":"RA-D1b","classification":"viable-extension","source_paths":["research/prime_lattice/findings/PL-159-fixed-step-suzuki-lower-recurrence-frontier.md","research/prime_lattice/findings/PL-160-attained-frontier-fixed-step-lower-escape.md","research/prime_lattice/findings/PL-161-fixed-step-pringsheim-frontier-phase-pinning.md"],"basis":"The fixed-step aliasing obstruction is sharpened rather than left generic: under RH failure, one-sided boundedness forces any surviving rightmost zero frontier to be unattained or recurrent and phase-pinned to the sampling identity, giving a precise zeta-specific anti-aliasing target."}
{"episode_id":"FE-2b7a9b-vis-farey-endpoint-controls","mode":"prospective","source_window_base":"cec27ab2ab7e14ef1ef8e3849412abd6171bd574","source_window_head":"2b7a9b6d8525663ee114e18eaee06419d6286f8a","line":"visual_exploration","atlas_territory":null,"classification":"known-prior-art","source_paths":["research/visual_exploration/findings/VIS-025-three-gap-pearson-fibers-correspondence-analysis.md","research/visual_exploration/findings/VIS-026-gap-permutation-discrepancy-bridge-covariance.md","research/visual_exploration/findings/VIS-027-farey-reflection-dirichlet-mode-filter.md","research/visual_exploration/findings/VIS-028-farey-endpoint-fan-forces-n-scale-spectrum.md","research/visual_exploration/findings/VIS-029-farey-fixed-nx-endpoint-totient-layers.md","research/visual_exploration/findings/VIS-030-farey-endpoint-profile-totient-riesz-remainder.md"],"basis":"The new visual residuals reduce to classical statistical, symmetry and arithmetic controls: correspondence/Pearson geometry, exact permutation/reflection nulls, the deterministic Farey endpoint fan, and finally a normalized-totient Riesz remainder with a Möbius decomposition. These become matched controls rather than independent evidence."}
