{"episode_id":"FE-2b7a9b-wi-singular-error-interface","mode":"prospective","source_window_base":"cec27ab2ab7e14ef1ef8e3849412abd6171bd574","source_window_head":"2b7a9b6d8525663ee114e18eaee06419d6286f8a","line":"weil_inertia","atlas_territory":"RA-B2b","classification":"new-barrier","source_paths":["research/weil_inertia/findings/WI-155-universal-loewner-lamzouri-lift-forces-real-gap-psd.md","research/weil_inertia/findings/WI-156-finite-adaptive-scalar-portfolios-stay-at-mt-barrier.md","research/weil_inertia/findings/WI-157-deweighted-finite-height-one-delta-has-only-log-squared-headroom.md","research/weil_inertia/findings/WI-158-bgstb-pointwise-error-is-not-uniform-on-singular-near-extremizers.md"],"basis":"Loewner lifts and finite adaptive scalar portfolios remain at the Montgomery-Taylor barrier, while the published BGSTB pointwise error is order-insufficient on singular near-extremizers. Any remaining support-one escape now requires new arithmetic control of the form-factor error or a genuinely different nonpositive/source-sensitive carrier."}
{"episode_id":"FE-2b7a9b-wp-resultant-positive-renormalization","mode":"prospective","source_window_base":"cec27ab2ab7e14ef1ef8e3849412abd6171bd574","source_window_head":"2b7a9b6d8525663ee114e18eaee06419d6286f8a","line":"weil_positivity","atlas_territory":"RA-C3","classification":"new-barrier","source_paths":["research/weil_positivity/findings/WP-146-critical-resultant-kernel-is-conditionally-indefinite-on-mixed-prime-three-chain.md","research/weil_positivity/findings/WP-147-disjoint-resultant-chains-force-unbounded-primitive-two-sided-inertia.md","research/weil_positivity/findings/WP-148-canonical-resultant-graph-laplacian-has-infinite-critical-degree-and-trivial-l2-domain.md","research/weil_positivity/findings/WP-149-spectator-prime-parallel-paths-collapse-resultant-resistance-and-energy-space.md","research/weil_positivity/findings/WP-150-local-finite-energy-renormalizations-erase-resultant-arithmetic-edges.md"],"basis":"The zero-order resultant selector has unavoidable mixed-prime inertia; its canonical positive graph completion has infinite fixed-shell degree and zero effective resistance through spectator primes, and every local positive renormalization that restores finite fixed-shell energy erases the original arithmetic edges."}
